  {
    "text": "Open-KNEAD is a training-free, locally deployable framework for meal nutrition estimation.",
    "topic": "Open-KNEAD framework"
  },
  {
    "text": "Open-KNEAD improves portion estimates over prior grounding methods and direct estimation in most backbone-dataset settings across two open MLLM families and three cuisines.",
    "topic": "Performance of Open-KNEAD"
  },
  {
    "text": "A modern Multimodal Large Language Model (MLLM) can directly estimate meal nutrition as accurately as or more accurately than a retrieval-augmented pipeline.",
    "topic": "MLLM nutrition estimation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Open-KNEAD uses a knowledge-grounded agentic framework for meal nutrition estimation.",
    "topic": "Knowledge-grounded agentic framework"
  },
  {
    "text": "Open-KNEAD is designed to be locally deployable without requiring training data.",
    "topic": "Local deployability of Open-KNEAD"
  }
]
